# .dockerignore for the CPPforAll judge.
#
# NOTE ON LOCATION: the judge is built with the REPO ROOT as the build context
#   (docker build -f judge/Dockerfile -t cppforall-judge .)
# Docker reads the ignore file from the CONTEXT ROOT, or — if present — the
# Dockerfile-adjacent "<dockerfile>.dockerignore". To make these rules apply with
# the root context, EITHER copy this file to the repo root as `.dockerignore`,
# OR (Docker 23+/BuildKit) keep it here renamed to `judge/Dockerfile.dockerignore`.
# The README documents this. The patterns below are written relative to the repo
# root so they work in whichever location you place them.

# ── Never ship the reference solutions in the build context ───────────────────
# (The Dockerfile also strips solution/ after the replay gate, but excluding the
# bulk of unrelated content keeps the context small and the build fast. We do NOT
# exclude content/drills/**/solution here because the build-time replay gate needs
# it; it is removed inside the image after the gate runs.)

# ── Site / app code the judge does not need ───────────────────────────────────
src/
public/
design/
docs/
scripts/
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
dist/
.astro/
src/generated/

# ── Notes (the judge only needs drills) ───────────────────────────────────────
content/notes/

# ── VCS / tooling / editor noise ──────────────────────────────────────────────
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.vscode/
.idea/
**/.DS_Store

# ── Build artifacts that might exist inside drills locally ────────────────────
content/drills/**/*.o
content/drills/**/*.dSYM/
content/drills/**/run
content/drills/**/cin_run
content/drills/**/starter/app
content/drills/**/solution/app
content/drills/**/tests/.*.txt
content/drills/**/tests/run
content/drills/**/__judge_*

# ── The judge's own dev cruft ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
judge/node_modules/
judge/*.log
